00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:39.400
price. Here is how it works when a contract pays on a number its holders can also trade.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:45.480
That setup is settlement manipulation. A paper posted to archive on June 30th models

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.280
contracts that settle on an asset price those holders can shove by trading the underlying.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.860
In the model, wealth moves from the liquidity traders in the prediction market to the manipulators.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.040
Price discovery in the underlying gets worse even while that market turns more liquid.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:07.300
After Polly Market listed a five-minute Bitcoin contract, spot-order flow jumped at settlement.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.280
Those jumps left large reversals once the contract had settled.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.560
The manipulators' profit was large, and most of it came from retail.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.460
The 15-minute versions largely did not show the same pattern.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:27.020
Stretching the horizon took the manipulation out, and the authors called out the design fix their model and their evidence both support.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:33.800
A second paper, posted to Archive on January 28th, mixes agent-based simulation with an

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.700
analytic account of the price path.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:41.620
Its betters differ in expertise, in noisy private information, in how fast they learn,

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.120
and in budget, and they watch public opinion before they bet.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.380
Across a wide parameter space, the simulated book stays stable.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:53.940
The tangle of behavior and prices produces self-regulatory discovery.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:58.880
A whale with a biased view of the value can still move the price, and the move does

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.800
not last forever.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:05.160
It gets bigger, and it hangs around longer, when the other bettors herd and learn slowly.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.620
The theory says the shove scales with the whale's share of the capital in the market.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:15.340
How long it lasts depends on how fast everyone else learns, and on how hard they herd.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.800
In this evidence, the defense fails on a short contract that settles on a tradable price.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:26.920
The longer horizon is the fix that first paper measured, a binary book can be pushed by

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:31.500
capital share and by hurting, then come back if the rest of the book keeps learning.

